  "placementWhy": "Scale bar (507 px = 1000 ft, 0.6012 m/px) and north up, shifted onto the three validated entrances. Mud-Raphael (both valid, 200.6 m apart in the DB) give 0.6058 m/px and -0.3 deg: the bar and north up hold; the free 3-point fit (0.560 m/px, -1.9 deg) is pulled by Muchachos, whose DB spot is only 15 m from Mud (41 m on the map). The plan length of the survey lines at the bar's scale (~9.8 km) matches the 9691 m surveyed. Checks: the 5 map-sourced DB points (validity unknown) all within 10 m (a consistent older georeference); the open-water pond by the N-S track (20.2593,-87.4862) sits on the Time Line passage's loop, and OSM's Cenote Santa Cruz pond is right beside the Muchachos/Mud entrances."
